### S1 | type: add | dimension: constructor | symbol: describe_entity
- Needs: n2 (t1:s1), n9 (t2:s6), n11 (t2:s8), n14 (t2:s14), n15 (t2:s16).
- Searches tried: widen "lettuce slice object description"; search "object description with sliced state and spatial location", "entity description state quantity location", "describe object with state and location"; lexical_label preserves only a leaf label, state_sliced is not a constructor, has_state/spatial_state assert attributed propositions, location_spec describes geographical addresses, and spatial_constraint alone is not a qualified entity selection.
- Typed parameters: label: TERM, state?: STRING, quantity?: NUMBER, portion?: BOOL, location?: TERM, relation?: STRING.
- Interpretation: Constructs a physical target selection description from a lexical_label term with optional source-supplied condition, count, material-portion flag, and spatial qualifier; quantity is a positive integer and counts selected objects or portions, portion=TRUE denotes parts of the labeled material, relation requires location and uses the accepted spatial-relation category, and state uses the accepted state-value category. Omitted attributes are unspecified; reuse denotes the same described target in a plan, not a fresh runtime selection or a continuously asserted location.
- Example: lexical_label(food_label::lettuce) followed by describe_entity(label=that_term, portion=TRUE, quantity=1, state=state_sliced) describes one slice of the labeled lettuce material; adding location=counter_term, relation=on restricts the selection to the counter.
- Contrast: A plain food_label::lettuce does not encode a slice, and a target selection description neither asserts existence nor creates a REF.
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_entity","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_entity(label: TERM, state?: STRING, quantity?: NUMBER, portion?: BOOL, location?: TERM, relation?: STRING) -> TERM","definition":"A physical target selection description based on a lexical_label term with source-supplied optional state, positive-integer count, material-portion flag, and location qualifier. State and relation use accepted state-value and spatial-relation categories; relation requires location, portion=TRUE selects parts of the labeled material, omissions are unspecified, and subsequent reuse denotes the same described target without asserting ongoing location or creating a REF.","not":"An assertion of existence, a new acquisition, or a physical runtime reference.","aliases":[]}

### S2 | type: add | dimension: member-family | symbol: describe_turn
- Needs: n1/n3 (t1:s1), n5 (t2:s2), n7 (t2:s4), n9 (t2:s6), n11 (t2:s8), n12 (t2:s10), n13 (t2:s12), n14 (t2:s14), n15 (t2:s16), n16 (t2:s18), n18 (t2:s20), n19 (t2:s22), n20 (t2:s24).
- Searches tried: widen each distinct action need text from n1,n3,n5,n7,n9,n11,n12,n13,n15,n16,n18,n19,n20; search "describe requested physical actions in a plan", "nonexecuting description pick up chill slice place physical procedure", "step forward left turn around single step", "direction left forward around single step", and "ordered sequence of described actions"; closest results are executable turn/walk/face/pick_up/slice/place/chill/remove, plus activity and sequence. Sequence supplies order but not the missing action semantics; activity lacks source, destination, direction, step count, traversal and placement-relation roles; walk_backward has the wrong direction.
- Shared category rules: These are pure primitive TERM constructors describing prospective physical actions, never operations or events; target/source/destination/traverse accept physical entity descriptions including lexical_label and describe_entity, not arbitrary terms merely because they type-check. Reused target terms track described identity within the plan without creating REF values, and omitted roles stay unspecified; no resources, outcomes or execution authorization are implied.
- Members: describe_turn — rotate body/view in a stated direction; describe_walk — locomotion with optional destination, direction, exact step count and across-space traversal; describe_face — orient toward the perceptible target; describe_pick_up — acquire the described target from an optional source; describe_slice — cut material into thin pieces while retaining described aggregate identity; describe_place — put the described target at a destination with a spatial relation; describe_chill — lower target temperature using an optional stated resource; describe_remove — take the described target out of an optional stated container.
- Exceptions: describe_turn directions are the explicitly governed STRING literals "left", "right", "around" (a half-turn), not operation names or entities. describe_walk directions are "forward", "backward", "left", "right" relative to the agent; steps is a positive integer count of walking steps without an inferred metric distance; traverse means across the supplied spatial region. describe_place relation uses accepted spatial-relation values; omitted destination in describe_chill represents a described request with unspecified resource, not an executable profile default.
- Example: describe_turn(direction="around"), describe_walk(direction="forward", steps=1), describe_face(target=lettuce_on_counter_description) composed by sequence represents turning around, stepping forward once, then facing the lettuce, without recording these acts as performed.
- Contrast: RECORD ACTION chill asserts a supplied occurrence; describe_chill only describes proposed cooling and does not assert that the food is cold.
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_turn","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_turn(direction: STRING) -> TERM","definition":"Describe rotation of the agent body/view. Direction accepts only the governed literals left, right, and around; around means a half-turn, and left/right supply no unstated angle.","not":"An executed turn or an orientation observation.","aliases":[]}
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_walk","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_walk(destination?: TERM, direction?: STRING, steps?: NUMBER, traverse?: TERM) -> TERM","definition":"Describe walking toward a physical destination, in an agent-relative direction, for an optional exact count of steps, or across a specified physical region. At least one argument is required; directions are forward/backward/left/right, steps is a positive integer without implied metric distance, traverse describes across-region traversal, and omitted roles remain unspecified.","not":"An executed movement, a teleportation, or an inferred distance.","aliases":[]}
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_face","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_face(target: TERM) -> TERM","definition":"Describe orienting the agent body/view directly toward the perceptible physical target description. Does not assert that the orientation occurred.","not":"A camera-gaze tilt or locomotion.","aliases":[]}
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_pick_up","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_pick_up(target: TERM, source?: TERM) -> TERM","definition":"Describe selecting and acquiring a physical target, optionally from the supplied source description. The selected identity remains a described target in the plan, never a runtime REF or evidence of acquisition.","not":"An acquisition event or implicit creation of an object.","aliases":[]}
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_slice","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_slice(target: TERM) -> TERM","definition":"Describe cutting the target material into thin pieces while retaining its described aggregate identity. No tool, quantity of resulting pieces, occurrence or outcome is supplied implicitly.","not":"Selecting an already sliced portion.","aliases":[]}
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_place","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_place(target: TERM, destination: TERM, relation?: STRING) -> TERM","definition":"Describe putting the identified physical target at the supplied physical destination, optionally in a specified accepted spatial-relation configuration. Does not reacquire the target, assert placement, or resolve an unstated left/right viewpoint.","not":"An executed place operation or mere dropping without a destination.","aliases":[]}
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_chill","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_chill(target: TERM, destination?: TERM) -> TERM","definition":"Describe lowering the physical target's temperature using the supplied cooling resource when stated. Omitted destination leaves the resource unspecified; the same described target identity is retained, and cooling duration, attained temperature and success are not implied.","not":"An assertion of cold state or an executable operation with an invented resource.","aliases":[]}
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_remove","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_remove(target: TERM, source?: TERM) -> TERM","definition":"Describe taking the physical target out of a container or enclosure, with source left unspecified when omitted. Refers to the same described target and neither asserts that removal occurred nor invents an enclosure.","not":"Destroying the target or deleting text.","aliases":[]}
